@Barry Ancona

I hang around with lawyers from time to time, since my wife is one, but I rarely talk about the law with them (although she certainly does).

I remember asking her back in July whether that term was a common one in everyday legal practice, and she said that it is rather rare.

@Steve L
Sometimes, a parallel can be a gulf. 
Up here, back when I practised, we still used the old Law Latin terms including writs of mandamus, certiorari and habeas corpus; a priori, (rarely) a posteriori, and a forteritori; and even the maxims. (The only one you may recognize is, "De minimis non curat lex." [The law is not concerned with trifles.]) But even in my day, Latin was already in decline.

